{
  "id": "28426_kosureru",
  "headword": "{擦|こす}れる",
  "reading": "こすれる",
  "romaji": "kosureru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb",
  "gloss": "to rub against; to chafe; to become worn",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to rub against (something); to chafe; to become worn",
      "explanation": "For two surfaces to rub against each other, often resulting in friction, irritation, or wear. The intransitive counterpart of {擦|こす}る (to rub something)."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "28426_kosureru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{靴|くつ}が{擦|こす}れて{痛|いた}い。",
      "english": "My shoes are rubbing and it hurts.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28426_kosureru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{袋|ふくろ}が{壁|かべ}に{擦|こす}れて{破|やぶ}れた。",
      "english": "The bag rubbed against the wall and tore.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "28426_kosureru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{長|なが}い{間|あいだ}{使|つか}っていたので、リュックの{底|そこ}が{擦|こす}れて{薄|うす}くなってきた。",
      "english": "Since I'd been using it for a long time, the bottom of the backpack had become worn and thin.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\nIntransitive ({自動詞|じどうし}). The transitive pair is {擦|こす}る (to rub something). The thing that rubs is marked with が; what it rubs against is marked with に.\n\nPATTERN:\n- AがBに{擦|こす}れる: A rubs against B\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {靴|くつ}が{擦|こす}れる: the shoes chafe\n- {肌|はだ}が{擦|こす}れる: the skin chafes\n- {生地|きじ}が{擦|こす}れる: the fabric gets worn\n- {擦|こす}れて{破|やぶ}れる: tear from friction\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {擦|こす}る: to rub (something) — the transitive pair; an actor deliberately rubs something\n- {擦|す}り{切|き}れる: to wear through completely — endpoint of long-term {擦|こす}れる",
